# Scenario 'monkey_camp_reg': monkey campaign, 28 segments of 6000 frames from freshly registered cartridge ('register': registered adapter, first-run tutorial pending).
# Generated by tools/trace/make_campaigns.py (deterministic). Every segment: power cycle (`reset`), boot, an optional fake-Internet fault
# (`net ...`), then `monkey <frames> <seed> <gap> <profile>` (seeded random taps; profiles mix a nav kb menu combo, see mgba_trace.c);
# a few segments unplug the adapter for a while (`unplug` / `plug`). The fake Internet has latency 2 frames, mails on the POP3 server
# and the richer synthetic web site (see scenarios.tsv). Purpose: breadth; absence of coverage proves nothing.
# --- segment 0: seed 10001 profile combo gap 16 faults http_status=500
wait 400
waitstable 60 max 600
net http_status=500
monkey 6000 10001 16 combo
# --- segment 1: seed 10008 profile a gap 32 faults tcp=refuse
reset
net pop_fail=none
net smtp_fail=none
net http_status=0
net http_missing=404
net http_trunc=-1
net http_nolen=0
net dns=ok
net tcp=ok
net cgi=none
wait 400
waitstable 60 max 600
net tcp=refuse
monkey 6000 10008 32 a
